Import stubs for the 1.14 EBOOT: the 24 imports KZ3 1.14 adds that had no handler in the patched tree (12
sceNpCommerce2, cellHttpCookie{Import,Export}WithClientId, cellSslCertGet{IssuerName,NameEntryCount,NameEntryInfo},
sceNpDrm{VerifyUpgradeLicense,ExecuteGamePurchase}, sceNpBasic{SetPresenceDetails2,GetFriendPresenceByIndex2},
sceNpManagerGetNetworkTime, sys_net_if_ctl, sys_crash_dump_set_user_log_area = sys_crashdump 0xB20F87B3). All are plain
C definitions that gen_hle_nids.py --all registers under ps3_compute_nid(name); every NID was checked against the 1.14
import table. Offline behaviour: store/request/result calls fail, the disc's upgrade license is reported present,
presence/network time answer offline, cookies form an empty jar, crash-dump areas are accepted and ignored. Also fixes
sceNpCommerce2CreateCtx's argument order (the context id is the 5th argument; the old form wrote it over the title's
handler descriptor). Each choice names its source (SDK behaviour or the 1.14 call site read with rizin) in a comment.
Tests: tools/assets/test_imports114.py (NID coverage), tools/assets/test_imports114.sh (return codes, host harness).
Upstream candidate (CreateCtx argument order; the stubs are general firmware coverage).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

